records.rationale:
In `SpanFlusher.join()`, the new multi-process loop breaks out of the *outer* `for` when the global `deadline` is exceeded:

```py
for process_index, process in self.processes.items():
    if deadline is not None:
        remaining_time = deadline - time.time()
        if remaining_time <= 0:
            break
    ...
    if isinstance(process, multiprocessing.Process):
        process.terminate()
```

This means if the deadline expires before iterating to later processes, those later processes will never reach the `terminate()` call. Pre-diff there was only one process and it always hit the t

